# fd's global ignore file (gitignore syntax). Unlike .gitignore, fd applies it
# outside git repos too, so it also covers searches from ~. The fzf widgets in
# ~/.config/fzf/fzf.bash list files through fd, so they skip these as well. A
# search rooted inside one of these directories still lists its contents.
#
# A pattern with a slash in the middle is anchored to the directory fd runs
# in, so multi-part paths start with **/ to match at any depth.

# Caches and package stores. The .rustup and .cargo entries cover the compat
# links that `dotfiles migrate tools` leaves in the home directory.
.cache/
.npm/
rustup/
.rustup/
**/cargo/registry/
**/.cargo/registry/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
.venv/

# fnm links back into its installed versions; the fzf widgets follow links
**/fnm/aliases/
fnm_multishells/

# Build output
build/
BUILD/
